<description>
Pack each color's foreground objects into bottom-aligned columns while preserving each object's shape.

Input structure
The grid has a dominant background color and two foreground color groups.
Each foreground color group contains exactly two monochromatic 4-connected
objects.

Rule
Order the color groups by their leftmost occupied column, creating output
columns from left to right with one background column between groups. Within
each color group, order its objects by decreasing bbox left column, crop
each object mask to its bbox, and stack those objects top-to-bottom in that
order with one background row between them. Bottom-align each color stack on
the original-size output canvas.

Key insight
Original position is used as ordering information: color groups sort
left-to-right, while objects inside a color sort right-to-left before being
repacked at the bottom.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "foreground color groups s ordered left-to-right by their leftmost pixel; within each group, its two 4-connected objects are ordered right-to-left by bbox left edge",
  "dst": "bottom-aligned color columns d left-to-right, with top-to-bottom stack slots inside each column",
  "match_cond": "rank(s.color_group left-to-right) == rank(d.column left-to-right); rank(s.object right-to-left) == rank(d.stack_slot top-to-bottom)",
  "transform": "crop each object mask to its bbox, preserve its color and shape, and paste it into its stack slot with one background row between objects and one background column between color groups"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10 [observed], background 0 [observed]
  foreground: exactly 2 colors, each with exactly 2 monochromatic 4-connected objects (4 objects total)
  objects:
    bbox: 1-3 rows x 2-5 cols, cell count 3-8, density 0.50-1.00
    separation: all objects pairwise non-adjacent (min Manhattan gap >= 2)
  ordering_constraints:
    within_color: the two objects must have distinct left-edge columns
    across_colors: the two color groups must have distinct minimum-left-edge values
  packing_constraints:
    packed_width: sum of each group's max-object-width + 1 gap column <= grid width
    stack_height: per group, sum of object heights + 1 gap row <= grid height (range 4-7)
  output_rule: |
    Sort color groups left-to-right by their min left-edge. Within each group,
    sort objects by descending left-edge. Stack objects top-to-bottom in that
    order (1 bg row gap between them), bottom-aligned to grid. Groups placed
    left-to-right (1 bg column gap), each group's column width = its max object width.

generation_strategy:
